---
description: Never declare Color values as const; use var instead
alwaysApply: true
---

# Colors are never constants

Do not declare `Color` values with `const`. Use `var` so colors can be tuned at runtime or in the inspector without fighting const restrictions.

```gdscript
# BAD
const COLOR_BROWN := Color.html("#918478")
const FALLBACK_COLOR := Color(0.57, 0.52, 0.47, 1.0)

# GOOD
var COLOR_BROWN := Color.html("#918478")
var FALLBACK_COLOR := Color(0.57, 0.52, 0.47, 1.0)
```

Non-color constants (sizes, paths, preloads, ints/floats) may still use `const`.
